Hi Matt,

Just to add to Marc Kéry's excellent answer, for your occupancy model
based on binary data, the goodness-of-fit statistic should be based on
aggregated data not the raw data. See rationale in McCullagh and Nelder
(1989. Generalized linear models, Chapman and Hall, p. 121). There are
different approaches on aggregating data to check goodness of fit, such
as over detection histories (the approach used by MacKenzie and Bailey
2004 and implemented in AICcmodavg), or over rows or columns (see
section 10.8 in Kéry and Royle 2016: AHM vol 1).

Best,

Marc
